{
  "schema": "narrative.live_barks/1",
  "_about": "Live barks (docs/ep/cloud-briefs/narrative-live-barks.md): the lines a fighter says in a match, at the beats the sim already emits as fx events. PRESENTATION ONLY: the emitter (NarrativeBarks, parked in docs/narrative/pending/live-barks/) reads the sim's events and never writes the sim, with its own seeded stream, so the golden is untouched. OFF BY DEFAULT: `enabled` is false. EVERY LINE here is an approved line: Orb's own words from homework 1, or Orb's marks on homework 11 (the 4 kept lines and the 26 rewrites that came from Gemini at Orb's direction, recorded under ai01). No line is invented for this file. The beats with no approved line are listed under `unmapped`, for Orb. Lines marked excluded wait on a swap or an event.",
  "enabled": false,
  "lines_policy": "approved",
  "seed_salt": 7301,
  "limits": {
    "per_fighter_gap_s": 8.0,
    "global_gap_s": 3.0,
    "line_cooldown_s": 180.0,
    "beat_cooldown_s": 12.0,
    "max_per_fighter_per_minute": 4,
    "after_ko_hush": true,
    "_about": "A fighter talks at most once every per_fighter_gap_s and at most max_per_fighter_per_minute a minute; any two barks are global_gap_s apart; no line repeats inside line_cooldown_s (a match is under 10 minutes, so a line plays once until the others are used); the same beat is held off for beat_cooldown_s. Silence is a feature (line-system.md)."
  },
  "display": {
    "style": "caption",
    "min_dur_s": 1.6,
    "max_dur_s": 2.6,
    "per_char_s": 0.035,
    "base_s": 0.9
  },
